## std.async.stream — AsyncStream trait + combinator stubs.
##
## From docs/spec.md §6.4.3: the `AsyncStream<T>` trait is the async
## analogue of `Iterator<T>`. Combinators (`map`, `filter`, `take`,
## `skip`, `chain`, `zip`, `buffered`, `timeout`, `collect`) are
## monomorphized at compile time and chain off the polling model.
##
## Stub: drops the `<T>` type parameter on the trait and uses a sync
## `poll_next` returning bool (Some/None flag) because the parser
## doesn't yet accept generic trait declarations with poll-style
## async return types. Once `async fun` lands, the trait gets a real
## `poll_next(self: *Self) -> Option<T>` shape.

pub trait AsyncStream {
    fun poll_next(self: *Self) -> bool;
}
